---

## Critical Design Constraints (Architect Refinements)

> [!CAUTION]
> These three rules prevent the most dangerous bugs in multiplayer frontends.

### 1. The Hook Handover (Single Source of Truth)
Only **one** polling loop may write to `useRaceStore` at any given time. The [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) must act as a switch:
```typescript
// RacePage.tsx — Only one heartbeat lives at a time.
const isLobbyPhase = gameState === 'WAITING_FOR_GUEST' || gameState === 'LOBBY_FULL' || gameState === 'READY_CHECK';

// useLobbyPolling runs during lobby, useRaceSync runs during race
// useLobbyPolling MUST clearInterval the exact ms state becomes COUNTDOWN
```
Without this, two intervals will fight over the Zustand store and cause UI flicker.

### 2. Persistence Idempotency (No Double-Saves)
Both players' frontends will call `saveResults()` when they see `FINISHED`. The backend's `PERSIST_LOCK` Lua script handles this, but the frontend **must** treat `ALREADY_SAVED` as a success:
```typescript
// In the save trigger logic:
if (result.status === 'SAVED' || result.status === 'ALREADY_SAVED') {
  store.persistenceStatus = 'SAVED'; // Both are success states
}
```
The "Loser" should never see a "Failed to Save" error.

### 3. Clock Offset in Lobby Hook
The countdown overlay depends on `target_start_ms` (server time). The **lobby hook** must calculate the clock offset *before* the race starts:
```typescript
// useLobbyPolling must do this on every poll response:
const clockOffsetMs = serverNowMs - Date.now();
store.setGameState({ clockOffsetMs });
```
Without this, the `CountdownOverlay` will be jittery or show wrong numbers.

---

## What Needs To Be Built

### Pages (2 Total)

You already have the core **RacePage**. You need **one new page**.

#### 1. [RacePage](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/app/race/%5BroomId%5D/page.tsx#23-224) — `/race/[roomId]` (EXISTS, NEEDS WIRING)
**What it does:** The multiplayer game board. Handles the full lifecycle from LOBBY → COUNTDOWN → IN_PROGRESS → FINISHED.

**What's missing on this page:**
- **Ready-Up UI**: A "Ready" button that appears when `state === 'LOBBY_FULL'`, calls `POST /api/race/ready`
- **Start Trigger**: Auto-triggered when both players ready up (the `READY_CHECK` response triggers `POST /api/race/multiplayer-start`)
- **Persistence Trigger**: When `state` transitions to `FINISHED`, automatically calls `POST /api/race/multiplayer/save`
- **Winner/Loser Display**: The [ResultsModal](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/components/ResultsModal.tsx#16-144) needs to show "You Won!" vs "You Lost!" based on `winnerId`

#### 2. `MultiplayerLobbyPage` — `/lobby` (NEW PAGE)
**What it does:** The entry point for multiplayer. Where users create or join rooms.

**Features:**
- **"Create Room" button**: Calls `POST /api/race/create`, gets back a `roomId`, then redirects to `/race/[roomId]`
- **"Join via Link" flow**: This already works — users navigate directly to `/race/[roomId]`, which triggers `PATCH /api/race/join` automatically
- **Active Room Display** (optional v2): Show rooms the user is currently in (via a heartbeat check)

> [!NOTE]
> The solo race page at `/(main)/(race)/solo-race` is completely separate and doesn't need changes.

---

### Services (1 New File)

#### [NEW] `multiplayerApi.ts` — `src/services/multiplayerApi.ts`
**Why:** Centralizes all multiplayer API calls in one place, mirroring the existing [raceApi.ts](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/services/raceApi.ts) pattern for solo.

**Methods needed:**

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|--------|----------|---------|
| `createRoom()` | `POST /api/race/create` | Creates a new room, returns `roomId` + `hostId` |
| `joinRoom(roomId)` | `POST /api/race/join` | Joins an existing room as guest |
| `readyUp(roomId, userId)` | `POST /api/race/ready` | Marks a player as ready |
| `startRace(roomId, userId)` | `POST /api/race/multiplayer-start` | Initiates the countdown (either player can trigger once both are ready) |
| `saveResults(roomId, guestId?)` | `POST /api/race/multiplayer/save` | Persists race results to Postgres |
| [getRoom(roomId)](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/lib/multiplayer/redis-room-service.ts#65-80) | `GET /api/race/[roomId]` | Fetches room state for rehydration |

---

### Hooks (2 Modifications)

#### [MODIFY] [useRaceSync.ts](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/hooks/useRaceSync.ts)
**Current behavior:** Polls `/api/race/sync` every 500ms and writes to Zustand.

**What to add:**
1. **Stop polling when `FINISHED`** — Currently it keeps polling after the race ends
2. **Trigger save on finish** — When `state` transitions to `FINISHED`, call `multiplayerApi.saveResults()` once. Treat both `SAVED` and `ALREADY_SAVED` as success states
3. **Guard against activation during lobby** — This hook must be disabled during `WAITING_FOR_GUEST`, `LOBBY_FULL`, `READY_CHECK` (the Hook Handover rule)

#### [NEW] `useLobbyPolling.ts` — `src/hooks/useLobbyPolling.ts`
**Why:** The Lobby phase (WAITING_FOR_GUEST → LOBBY_FULL → READY_CHECK) needs its own polling loop, separate from the high-frequency race sync.

**Behavior:**
- Polls `GET /api/race/[roomId]` every 2-3 seconds (much slower than sync)
- Updates the store with the room state so the Lobby UI is reactive
- **Calculates clock offset** on every response: `clockOffsetMs = serverNowMs - Date.now()`
- **Hard stop** once `state === 'COUNTDOWN'` — must `clearInterval` immediately so [useRaceSync](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/hooks/useRaceSync.ts#23-103) becomes the sole writer
- Detects opponent disconnection via [heartbeat](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/lib/multiplayer/redis-room-service.ts#134-163) data

---

### Store Modifications (1 Modification)

#### [MODIFY] [useRaceStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/store/useRaceStore.ts)
**Current fields that already work:** `state`, `opponentProgress`, `opponentWpm`, `winnerId`, `isReady`, `localFinished`, `clockOffsetMs`, `targetStartMs`

**What to add:**

| Field | Type | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| `role` | `'host' \| 'guest' \| null` | Identifies this client's role for UI labeling and debug |
| `hostReady` | `boolean` | Display host ready status in lobby |
| `guestReady` | `boolean` | Display guest ready status in lobby |
| `opponentName` | `string \| null` | Display in [GhostCar](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/components/game/GhostCar.tsx#8-11) name tag |
| `persistenceStatus` | `'IDLE' \| 'SAVING' \| 'SAVED' \| 'ALREADY_SAVED' \| 'ERROR'` | Tracks save state for [ResultsModal](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/components/ResultsModal.tsx#16-144) |

---

### Components (Modifications + 1 New)

#### [MODIFY] [ResultsModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rnasy/Desktop/Typeracing/src/components/ResultsModal.tsx)
**What to add:**
- **Winner/Loser banner**: Use `winnerId` vs `userId` to show "VICTORY" or "DEFEAT"
- **Opponent stats**: Show opponent's WPM alongside yours for comparison
- **Rematch button** (optional v2): Placeholder for future rematch flow
- **Persistence feedback**: Show "Saving..." → "Saved!" using `persistenceStatus` from store

#### [NEW] `ReadyUpOverlay.tsx` — `src/components/game/ReadyUpOverlay.tsx`
**What it does:** Replaces the current static "Awaiting Opponent" overlay when both players are in the room.

**UI States:**

```
WAITING_FOR_GUEST  →  "Share the link. Awaiting opponent..."  (existing overlay, keep as-is)
LOBBY_FULL         →  [Ready Up] button for each player, shows ready status badges
READY_CHECK        →  "Both players ready! Starting..." (auto-triggers countdown via API)
```

